{"p":{"slug":"allan-julie","first":"Allan","last":"Julie","cc":"SEY","iso":"sc","country":"Seychelles","g":0,"img":"https://platform.worldofsailors.com/storage/uploads/2026/08/3-allan-julie-5-1786263134.webp","cm":180,"kg":104,"bio":"My name is Allan julie. and I am from of the Seychelles. I am a passionate and dedicated sailor, currently serving as the captain of the Seychelles SSL Gold Club Team. Throughout my sporting career, I have had the honor of representing my country at seven Olympic Games, a journey that has been one of the greatest achievements of my life. Over the years, I have also won several medals at African Championships and have been recognized as Seychelles' Best Sportsman on seven occasions. These accomplishments reflect my commitment, perseverance, and love for sport. Sailing has been a major part of my life for more than 20 years. Today, I continue to enjoy the sport by racing a FarEast 28 yacht with my friends. We participate in many weekend regattas and enjoy the camaraderie and excitement that sailing brings. Beyond competitive sailing, I have a strong interest in windsurfing and canoeing, both of which allow me to stay connected to the ocean and maintain an active lifestyle. In my free time, I enjoy playing dominoes with friends at the beach near my home. The friendly competition and social atmosphere make it one of my favorite ways to relax. Looking back on my journey, I am proud of what I have achieved in sport and grateful for the opportunities I have had to represent Seychelles on the international stage. My passion for sailing remains as strong as ever, and I continue to embrace new challenges both on and off the water.","soc":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/allan.julie.7/"},"rk":{"s":[3237,333.67,3230,"2026-11-24",[1053,"2020-10-13"]]},"st":{"ev":9,"win":0,"pod":1,"avg":37.1,"best":2},"cls":["Finn","ILCA 7","SSL 47"],"recn":5},"res":{"s":[["2026-06-04","African & Oceanian Qualifiers - SSL Gold Cup 2026","Lac de Neuchâtel","SUI